  "description": "Named after one of San Diego's finest street spots, the Dana features an all chromoly frame with responsive geometry, a short 12.75\" rear end and a 20.5\" top tube to fit the mid-sized crew. Back that up with an all chromoly fork, 9\" rise bars and 165mm cranks and you're rolling strong. Premium CK 2.4\" tires mounted on double-wall rims with sealed front and cassette rear hubs, a half-link chain and a set of pegs included--ready to go.\nFull chromoly frame with removable brake mounts and mid BB shell; 20.5\" top tube\nFull chromoly 2-piece steerer fork with tapered legs intenrally threaded steerer tube; 25mm offset\nHaro full chromoly 9\" rise bars\nHaro Baseline stem\nPremium CK grips\nHaro Baseline chromoly 8-spline 19mm cranks; 165mm length\nSealed front and cassette rear hub laced to 36H double wall rims\n25/9 gear ratio\nHaro Baseline half-link chain\nPremium CK 2.4\" Tires",
